  "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $9?$\n\nI. $34\\,154\\,119$\n\nII. $9\\,173\\,589$\n\nIII. $733\\,123$",
  "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $9$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $34\\,154\\,119$ is\n\n$$\n3+4+1+5+4+1+1+9=28,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $34\\,154\\,119$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $9\\,173\\,589$ is\n\n$$\n9+1+7+3+5+8+9=42,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $9\\,173\\,589$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $733\\,123$ is\n\n$$\n7+3+3+1+2+3=19,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $733\\,123$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
